          ch = (ch - 'a' + 13) % 26 + 'a';
          printf("%c", ch);
        }
[A-Z]   { char ch = yytext[0];
          ch = (ch - 'A' + 13) % 26 + 'A';
          printf("%c", ch);
        }
%%
void main(void){
    yylex();
}
```

Compiling above with `flex` results in `lex.yy.c`, in which C function `yylex()` implements the rules and which literally includes the user functions. The main function calls `yylex()`, so no user code is needed here. The file `lex.yy.c` is compiled with `cc` to an executable file, here called `rot13`:

```python
